# UI conventions

- Build a clean, responsive, accessible storefront and admin area.
- Prioritize clear hierarchy, readable text, consistent spacing and predictable navigation.
- Use a small shared set of buttons, inputs, cards, tables, dialogs and feedback components.
- Forms show field-level validation errors and submission/loading state.
- Destructive actions require confirmation.
- Provide loading skeletons or clear loading indicators, empty states, retryable errors and success feedback.
- Do not over-animate. Avoid decorative complexity that harms performance or course readability.
- Do not invent extra product requirements or screens.
